/T (Two warnings come from these plots. Hindi messages are 78.3 % scam against 62.8 % for English, because only a few Hindi and Marathi legitimate templates exist; a model could learn 'Devanagari script = scam', so per-language results must be reported separately. The message type \(sms, e-mail, offer\) is almost uninformative \(64-67 % scam\). Finally, the scenario plot shows that nearly every scenario belongs to one class only - this is the leakage examined in Step 13. )
/E (Two warnings come from these plots. Hindi messages are 78.3 % scam against 62.8 % for English, because only a few Hindi and Marathi legitimate templates exist; a model could learn 'Devanagari script = scam', so per-language results must be reported separately. The message type \(sms, e-mail, offer\) is almost uninformative \(64-67 % scam\). Finally, the scenario plot shows that nearly every scenario belongs to one class only - this is the leakage examined in Step 13. )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [59]
>>
