2685 0 obj
<<
/Title (Two components explain only 50.1 % of the variance\(34.2 % + 15.9 %\), so PCA compresses these ten columns only moderately. PCA_1 is loaded by url_risk_max \(0.42\), n_words \(0.40\), lex_total \(0.40\) and has_url \(0.39\) - a 'scam-signal intensity' axis - andPCA_2 mainly by n_digits \(0.65\) and bait_score. K-Means found four groups without seeing the label.Cluster 0 \(729 messages\) is 100 % scam, with a mean URL risk of 0.71 and 4.8 lexicon hits; cluster 2 \(680 messages\) is only 32.6 % scam and has almost no URL risk. This works as a behaviour feature, but the perfect purityofcluster 0 reflects how clean the synthetic templates are.)
/Dest [26 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2473 0 R
/Prev 2803 0 R
>>
endobj
2686 0 obj
<<
/Title (Code)
/Dest [26 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2474 0 R
/Next 2804 0 R
>>
endobj
2687 0 obj
<<
/Title (Figure 14: Feature selection - mutual information and chi-square rankings)
/Dest [27 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2474 0 R
/Prev 2805 0 R
>>
endobj
2688 0 obj
<<
/Title (Both filters agree on the picture: lexicon strength \(lex_total\) is the most informativefeature by mutual information \(0.51\), while chi-square ranks the URL features highest \(n_no_https,url_risk_max, n_susp_tld\). The two top chi-square scores are identical because risky_url flags exactly the same rows as n_no_https, so one of them \(risky_url\) is dropped as a duplicate.)
/Dest [27 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2269 0 R
/Prev 2474 0 R
/Next 2689 0 R
>>
endobj
2689 0 obj
<<
/Title (Three near-constant columns \(n_repeated_words, n_at, url_max_digits\) hold one value in at least 99 % of the rows and are removed.)
/Dest [27 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2269 0 R
