/Title (Because the data has no gaps, 10 % of n_words was hidden on purpose and four imputers tried to recover it. KNN is far better \(MAE 0.82\) than mean \(4.94\), median \(4.95\) and mode \(5.44\), because n_words is correlated with n_special \(0.70\) and n_chars \(0.61\), and KNN uses those neighbours while the other three ignore them. Mean and median would win on a skewed count column that has no correlated partners, so the technique must be chosen from the data - not by habit.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2907 0 R
/Prev 2937 0 R
>>
